# Optimal-control / HJB math layer

This rule scopes the JAX-compiled optimal-control core, the
Lucic-Tse portfolio options market-maker, and the hftbacktest LOB
engine. Narrative: [aqp_docs/optimal-control.md](mdc:aqp_docs/optimal-control.md),
[aqp_docs/portfolio-options-mm.md](mdc:aqp_docs/portfolio-options-mm.md),
[aqp_docs/hft-backtest.md](mdc:aqp_docs/hft-backtest.md),
[aqp_docs/microstructure-toxicity.md](mdc:aqp_docs/microstructure-toxicity.md).

## Hard rules

1. **Single solver entry-point per problem.** New AvSt logic ships
   inside [aqp/optimal_control/avellaneda_stoikov.py](mdc:aqp/optimal_control/avellaneda_stoikov.py)
   exposed via ``compute_optimal_quotes`` / ``glft_closed_form`` /
   ``quote_grid``. New CJ logic ships inside
   [aqp/optimal_control/cartea_jaimungal.py](mdc:aqp/optimal_control/cartea_jaimungal.py)
   exposed via ``solve`` / ``optimal_trading_rate`` /
   ``optimal_liquidation_value``. New Lucic-Tse logic ships inside
   [aqp/options/portfolio_mm.py](mdc:aqp/options/portfolio_mm.py).
   Don't open-code the math inside a strategy / env / agent body.
2. **JAX kernels stay pure.** Functions decorated with ``@jax.jit``
   take only static-or-traced inputs and contain no I/O, no globals,
   no Python control flow keyed on traced values. The wrapper public
   functions can do all the orchestration; the inner kernel must be
   trace-compatible.
3. **No Python `for` loops in matrix ops.** Lucic-Tse uses
   ``jnp.einsum`` and broadcasted ops only. AvSt grid evaluation uses
   ``jax.vmap``. The fast path through these solvers is what makes
   the closed forms tractable in real time.
4. **Analysis flows write to gold tier.** The flows in
   [aqp/analysis/flows/optimal_control.py](mdc:aqp/analysis/flows/optimal_control.py)
   live under namespace ``optimal_control`` so
   ``AnalysisRuntime`` writes to ``aqp_gold_analysis_optimal_control``
   per AGENTS rule 21. Don't override ``output_namespace`` to write
   anywhere else.
5. **Agents call the math through DataMCPTools.** The four agent-
   facing tools are ``data.optimal_control.solve_hjb``,
   ``data.optimal_control.evaluate_strategy``,
   ``data.optimal_control.list_regimes``, and
   ``data.strategy_config.update``. Add new tools under
   [aqp/data/mcp/tools/optimal_control.py](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/optimal_control.py)
   or [aqp/data/mcp/tools/strategy_config.py](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/strategy_config.py);
   register via ``@register_data_mcp_tool``. Per AGENTS rule 22,
   agents NEVER read Iceberg / Postgres / Redis directly.
6. **Whitelist all writes.** ``data.strategy_config.update`` only
   accepts a small set of fields (``gamma``, ``sigma``, ``kappa``,
   ``k``, ``gamma_inv``, ``base_spread``, ``order_size``,
   ``max_position``). Adding a new whitelisted field requires an ADR
   note documenting the threat model and the lineage event the change
   produces.
7. **HFT progress emits use the canonical frame.** The
   [run_lob_backtest](mdc:aqp/tasks/hft_tasks.py) task emits
   ``{task_id, stage, message, timestamp, **extras}`` with the extras
   ``events_processed`` / ``equity`` / ``position``. Adding fields to
   ``extras`` is fine; renaming is not (AGENTS rule 4).
8. **RL envs auto-register through the metaclass.** Set ``rl_kind``
   and ``rl_alias`` (and optional ``rl_tags`` / ``rl_source`` /
   ``rl_category``); the
   [`RLComponent`](mdc:aqp/rl/core/base.py) metaclass calls
   ``register`` for you. Don't decorate manually.

## Optional dependency hygiene

- Pure-Python fallbacks for AvSt / CJ ship alongside the JAX paths so
  the modules import cleanly without ``[optimal-control]``.
- ``aqp/options/greeks_jax.py`` returns ``None`` when neither JAX nor
  ``fast_vollib`` are installed; ``aqp.analysis.pricing.greeks_grid``
  routes through it and falls back to the SciPy double-loop.
- ``aqp/backtest/hft.py`` imports ``hftbacktest`` lazily inside
  ``run`` and raises ``ImportError`` with install instructions when
  the extra is missing.

## Don't

- Don't import ``hftbacktest`` at module top in any AQP file. Lazy-
  import inside the function that uses it.
- Don't call ``litellm.completion`` / ``OllamaClient`` directly from
  these modules — agent / RL bodies use ``router_complete`` per
  AGENTS rule 2.
- Don't write to a non-``aqp_gold_analysis_optimal_control``
  namespace from a flow registered under namespace ``optimal_control``.
- Don't bypass ``data.strategy_config.update``'s whitelist by adding
  a sibling tool that writes a different YAML field.
- Don't replace the ``MarketMakingEnv`` registration alias. The
  graduated env keeps ``rl_alias = "MarketMakingEnv"`` so existing
  configs keep loading; the legacy stylised env survives as
  ``MarketMakingStubEnv``.

## When in doubt

1. Read [aqp_docs/optimal-control.md](mdc:aqp_docs/optimal-control.md) for the
   math.
2. Read the relevant scoped rule:
   - [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) hard rules — full list.
   - [tasks-api.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/tasks-api.mdc) — Celery + REST
     layering.
   - [data-mcp.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/data-mcp.mdc) — DataMCP boundary.
3. Search the code: ``rg "compute_optimal_quotes|compute_lucic_tse_quotes|LobBacktestEngine" aqp/``.
4. Still stuck → ask. Don't guess and ship.
